            <ArticleTitle>Highly Diastereo- and Enantioselective Palladium-Catalyzed [3 + 2] Cycloaddition of Vinyl Epoxides and α,β-Unsaturated Ketones.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>6658-6661</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.orglett.7b03386</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An asymmetric [3 + 2] cycloaddition reaction of vinyl epoxides with α,β-unsaturated ketones, the single activated electron-deficient alkenes, has been achieved under Pd-catalysis in excellent diastereo- and enantioselectivity. The utilities of the protocol are demonstrated by transformation of the products into other useful chiral molecules. Density functional theory calculations rationalize the stereocontrol of the reaction.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
